    <item>
      <title>Deploying Your First Site</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/</guid>
      <description>&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/01-netlify-homepage.png&#34;alt=&#34;Netlify homepage&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Netlify homepage&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Visit &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://www.netlify.com/&#34;&gt;https://www.netlify.com/&lt;/a&gt; and click the &amp;lsquo;Sign up&amp;rsquo; button in the top navigation&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/02-netlify-signup.png&#34;alt=&#34;Netlify sign up page&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Netlify sign up page&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Choose &amp;lsquo;GitHub&amp;rsquo; on the sign up page&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;If you are logged out of GitHub, then log in&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/03-github-account-permissions.png&#34;alt=&#34;Granting GitHub account permissions to Netlify&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Granting GitHub account permissions to Netlify&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Read the permissions and click the &amp;lsquo;Authorize netlify&amp;rsquo; button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;If prompted to &amp;lsquo;Tell us about yourself&amp;rsquo;, fill out the information. Note: only the &amp;lsquo;I&amp;rsquo;m using Netlify for&amp;rsquo; question is required, so you can skip everything else if you want&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/04-deploy-first-project.png&#34;alt=&#34;Choose how to deploy your site on Netlify&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Choose how to deploy your site on Netlify&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Click the &amp;lsquo;Import from Git&amp;rsquo; button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/05-git-provider.png&#34;alt=&#34;Choose your sites Git provider on Netlify&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Choose your sites Git provider on Netlify&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;When asked to connect a Git provider, click the &amp;lsquo;GitHub&amp;rsquo; button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/06-github-further-permissions.png&#34;alt=&#34;Granting further GitHub permissions to Netlify&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Granting further GitHub permissions to Netlify&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;A pop-up window will ask for some more GitHub permissions. Click the &amp;lsquo;Authorize Netlify&amp;rsquo; button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/07-install-netlify.png&#34;alt=&#34;Installing Netlify into your GitHub account&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Installing Netlify into your GitHub account&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;You will be asked to &amp;lsquo;Install Netlify&amp;rsquo;. If you are prompted &amp;lsquo;Where do you want to install Netlify&amp;rsquo;, choose &lt;em&gt;your personal&lt;/em&gt; GitHub username.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;section class=&#34;c-note c-note--warning&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;h4 class=&#34;c-note__title e-heading__4&#34;&gt;⚠️Warning&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/h4&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;c-note__text &#34;&gt;Do &lt;strong&gt;NOT&lt;/strong&gt; choose Code Your Future&amp;rsquo;s account, as this won&amp;rsquo;t work!&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/section&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/08-choose-repo.png&#34;alt=&#34;Choosing the GitHub repo to create your site from&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Choosing the GitHub repo to create your site from&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Select the GitHub repo to create a site from&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/09-choose-branch.png&#34;alt=&#34;Choosing the branch to create your site from&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Choosing the branch to create your site from&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Under &amp;lsquo;Branch to deploy&amp;rsquo; choose the &amp;lsquo;main&amp;rsquo; branch of your repo, which is usually called &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt;. You do not need to change anything under &amp;lsquo;Customize build settings&amp;rsquo;, Netlify will do this for you&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Click the &amp;lsquo;Deploy site&amp;rsquo; button&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;It may take a few minutes before the deploy is complete. Try refreshing your browser, when a &lt;code&gt;.netlify.app&lt;/code&gt; URL appears then the site is live&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/first-site/10-site-is-live.png&#34;alt=&#34;The site is live&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;The site is live&#34;/&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Deploying Another Site</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/another-site/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/another-site/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;first-log-into-netlifyhttpswwwnetlifycom&#34;&gt;First: log into &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://www.netlify.com/&#34;&gt;Netlify&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;section class=&#34;c-note c-note--tip&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;h4 class=&#34;c-note__title e-heading__4&#34;&gt;💡Remember&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/h4&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;c-note__text &#34;&gt;Remember that you sign in using GitHub.&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/section&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/another-site/01-netlify-dashboard.png&#34;alt=&#34;Netlify dashboard&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Netlify dashboard&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;On your Netlify dashboard, click Sites in the top navigation&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/another-site/02-sites-page.png&#34;alt=&#34;Creating a new site from an existing project&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Creating a new site from an existing project&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Click on the &amp;lsquo;Add new site&amp;rsquo; button, then &amp;lsquo;Import an existing project&amp;rsquo;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/another-site/03-git-provider.png&#34;alt=&#34;Choosing your sites Git provider&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Choosing your sites Git provider&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;This might be familiar now! Click &amp;lsquo;GitHub&amp;rsquo; as your Git provider&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Deploying Express</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/deploying-backends/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/deploying-backends/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-what-are-netlify-functions&#34;&gt;🔌 What are Netlify Functions?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://docs.netlify.com/functions/overview/&#34;&gt;Netlify Functions&lt;/a&gt; allow us to deploy some backend systems. This feature is designed for serverless frameworks, but supports Express.JS as well with some limitations.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-how-to-organise-your-files&#34;&gt;🗂️ How to organise your files&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To deploy an Express.JS backend to Netlify you need to make sure that your backend meets the following requirements:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;-checklist&#34;&gt;✅ Checklist&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;input disabled=&#34;&#34; type=&#34;checkbox&#34;&gt; &lt;strong&gt;All of your backend paths start with &lt;code&gt;/api&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;. For example &lt;code&gt;/api/videos&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/api/bookings/1&lt;/code&gt;, etc. Every other URL will be considered as part of the frontend.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;input disabled=&#34;&#34; type=&#34;checkbox&#34;&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Your backend code is organised&lt;/strong&gt; like this:&#xA;a. &lt;code&gt;/server/api.js&lt;/code&gt; contains your actual backend functionality. You can include other modules from this file if you wish to split the file into multiple modules. This file is used by Netlify.&#xA;a. &lt;code&gt;/server/server.js&lt;/code&gt; starts up your express.js server and contain settings to load up &lt;code&gt;api.js&lt;/code&gt; to serve everything under &lt;code&gt;/api&lt;/code&gt;. This file is used for local development.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;input disabled=&#34;&#34; type=&#34;checkbox&#34;&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Your backend does not use global variables to save data&lt;/strong&gt; between requests. All persistence is done through the database or by using cookies.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Once you have checked your backend meets the requirements, you are ready to add support for Netlify.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Common Problems</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/common-problems/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/common-problems/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;my-site-is-not-updating-when-i-push-a-change-to-github&#34;&gt;My site is not updating when I push a change to GitHub&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Are you sure that you are pushing to the same branch that Netlify is &amp;ldquo;watching&amp;rdquo;?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Be aware that changes can take a few minutes to show up&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Check the logs under the Deploy tab. If there is an error, Netlify won&amp;rsquo;t be able to deploy your site&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;my-repo-doesnt-show-up-in-the-netlify-menu&#34;&gt;My repo doesn&amp;rsquo;t show up in the Netlify menu&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Follow the prompt to configure your Netlify-GitHub integration and give it access to the repo you need (or all repos).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-site-is-using-the-wrong-repo-or-wrong-github-account&#34;&gt;The site is using the wrong repo or wrong GitHub account&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Delete &amp;amp; recreate your site.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Renaming Your Site</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/renaming-site/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/renaming-site/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Once you have a site deployed, you may notice that Netlify has created a randomised &lt;code&gt;.netlify.app&lt;/code&gt; URL to access it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You may want to change this to a &amp;ldquo;friendlier&amp;rdquo; URL so that it is easier to remember and share. We also ask you to change the URL of sites you create for coursework, so that it is easier for volunteers to find your site and give feedback. See &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;../site-naming-conventions&#34;&gt;website naming conventions&lt;/a&gt; for rules to name your site.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Site Naming Conventions</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/site-naming-conventions/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/netlify/site-naming-conventions/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;To make it easier for teachers and volunteers to find and review your homework,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;!-- CYF-ONLY --&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;All CYF coursework projects should be hosted with the following naming scheme:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;cyf-USERNAME-PROJECT_NAME&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&amp;hellip;where:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;USERNAME&lt;/code&gt; is your GitHub username&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;PROJECT_NAME&lt;/code&gt; is the name of the coursework project. If you are not sure, then ask!&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Examples for the project called &lt;code&gt;cakes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;cyf-nbogie-cakes&lt;/code&gt;.netlify.app&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;cyf-40thieves-cakes&lt;/code&gt;.netlify.app&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;cyf-kkarimi-cakes&lt;/code&gt;.netlify.app&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Examples for the project called &lt;code&gt;photo-gallery&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;cyf-lucymac-photo-gallery&lt;/code&gt;.netlify.app&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;cyf-textbook-photo-gallery&lt;/code&gt;.netlify.app&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
